From ab11a6088018c474609f8ad85315441b28b60346 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 13:47:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07191/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-10: budget cannot
 help induction fire -- exploration exhaustion, not action count

Closes the last open hypothesis from REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-9: does a much
larger budget give the pre-LLM-induction trust-check gates enough
transitions to clear? Answer: no, and not for the reason assumed.

Ran --induction --budget 250 on sp80 (the untested combination).
Still real_max_level_observed=0 -- but the decisive finding is in
induction_attempts: exactly ONE attempt, at transition_count=25,
byte-identical to the budget=46 run, despite 242 real actions
consumed (near-full budget). Induction never got a second chance,
let alone more transitions to learn from.

Traced to source (arc_competition_agent.py:3261-3293): the trigger
is len(self.transitions) >= self.explore_budget OR self.explorer.
explored_out, and explored_out (StepwiseExplorer._frontier() is
None) means the graph-explorer's frontier of untested candidate
states is genuinely empty -- a property of the game's reachable-
state graph size from this harness's generic domain-blind explorer,
not of the budget ceiling. sp80's frontier exhausts at ~25
transitions regardless of whether 46 or 250 actions are available;
extra budget past that point goes to whatever non-induction fallback
follows the skipped attempt, not to gathering fresh transitions.

Added explorer_explored_out to the artifact schema (run_game() reads
policy.explorer.explored_out directly) so future runs can check this
without re-deriving it from induction_attempts' transition count.

Every reasonably-cheap lever this investigation has tried is now
exhausted: router choice (5699-6), budget (5699-7), induction
re-enablement (5699-8/9/10), and the codebase's own documented
trust-metric override (5699-9) -- none move the headline result on
this specific 4-game/stripped-config harness. What remains is
structural: re-enabling one of the other still-disabled features
(frame-change scorer, goal-bias, go-explore archive), or accepting
this harness's generic explorer doesn't generate enough distinct
transitions on these games for any trust-gated mechanism to engage,
independent of budget, router, or induction settings.

2 new tests (explorer_explored_out defaults honestly when absent,
spec-declaration). Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-10 with its own scenario.

